## jantar's VM flags.
##
## -noinput: the release never reads stdin (as a service its stdin is the tty).
-noinput

## Battery: by default an idle scheduler busy-waits ("spins") a short while
## before sleeping, in case work arrives. For a dashboard that wakes a few
## times a second, that spinning is wasted CPU and wakeups. Turn it off for
## normal, dirty CPU and dirty I/O schedulers.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none


## File names are UTF-8 whatever the locale (a service may have none).
+fnu

## One scheduler of each kind, not one per core. jantar's work is a few small
## samples a second and a 2-4 ms frame at most 4 times a second; with 16
## schedulers, idle ones keep waking to look for work to steal, and there is
## never enough to share. Measured over a minute with the dashboard hidden on
## a 16-core machine (default 48 threads -> 9):
##   default             770 ms CPU/min, 121 wakeups/s
##   +S 2 (2 dirty each) 690 ms,         106/s
##   +S 1 (1 dirty each) 640 ms,          83/s
+S 1:1
+SDcpu 1:1
+SDio 1
